cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WorkflowSim-yixin in research, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "WorkflowSim-yixin: an auditable discrete-event simulator for scientific workflow scheduling research"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "WorkflowSim-yixin contributors"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-02"
license: "GPL-2.0-or-later"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yixin0724/workflowsim-research"
url: "https://github.com/yixin0724/workflowsim-research"
abstract: >-
  A discrete-event simulator for research on scientific workflow scheduling that
  treats evidence as a first-class product. Every run emits a manifest, metrics,
  and an event stream whose numbers are independently recomputable by a Python
  auditor; energy, carbon, and DVFS accounting follow declared conservation laws
  and are locked by frozen benchmarks, mutation gates, and an offline report.
keywords:
  - scientific workflows
  - workflow scheduling
  - discrete-event simulation
  - reproducibility
  - energy accounting
  - carbon accounting
  - DVFS
  - cloud computing